### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 03 — SESSION LIFECYCLE: CREATE → RUN → STATUS → TERMINATE
###
### Full happy-path flow for a synchronous and asynchronous agent run.
###
### Endpoint map (all under /api/v1):
###   POST   /sessions                     → create session (201)
###   POST   /sessions/{id}/run            → run agent synchronously (200/202/408/4xx/5xx)
###   POST   /sessions/{id}/run-async      → run agent async, returns immediately (202)
###   GET    /sessions/{id}/status/{role}  → poll checkpoint state (200 / 404)
###   DELETE /sessions/{id}               → terminate session (204)
###
### Response shapes:
###   run/run-async (Finished)         → {answer, totalInputTokens, totalOutputTokens}
###   run/run-async (AwaitingApproval) → {toolName, paramsJson, sessionId}  HTTP 202
###   run/run-async (LoopExceeded)     → {reason, code:"LOOP_EXCEEDED"}     HTTP 408
###   run/run-async (Failed/Budget)    → {reason, code:"BUDGET"}            HTTP 429
###   run/run-async (Failed/Denied)    → {reason, code:"USER_DENIED"}       HTTP 422
###   status                           → {sessionId, status, steps[], failReason}
###     status values: IN_PROGRESS | AWAITING_APPROVAL | COMPLETED | FAILED | COMPROMISED
###
### Prerequisites: ArcClaw running in serve mode, GROQ_API_KEY set
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
@validKey = key-internal-changeme

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 1 — CREATE SESSION
# Returns a fresh UUID-based sessionId. No DB writes yet — just a
# heartbeat registration.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SESSION-1] Create a new session
# @name mainSession
# Expect 201: {"sessionId": "xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 2a — SYNCHRONOUS RUN (blocks until agent finishes)
# The HTTP connection stays open until the agent loop completes.
# Ideal for short tasks (maxIterations ≤ 3).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SESSION-2] Run agent synchronously — simple arithmetic (no tools needed)
# Expect 200: {"answer": "4", "totalInputTokens": N, "totalOutputTokens": N}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{mainSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What is 2 + 2? Answer with just the number.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 2
}

###

### [SESSION-3] Check status after sync run
# Expect 200: {"sessionId":"...","status":"COMPLETED","steps":[...],"failReason":null}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{mainSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 2b — ASYNCHRONOUS RUN (returns immediately; poll status)
# The HTTP response returns once the virtual thread is spawned.
# Use /status/{role} to poll the checkpoint until COMPLETED or FAILED.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SESSION-4] Create a second session for async test
# @name asyncSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SESSION-5] Run agent asynchronously
# Returns immediately: {"answer":"...","totalInputTokens":N,"totalOutputTokens":N}
# or HTTP 202 AwaitingApproval if a tool needs HITL
# For a deeper task, increase maxIterations
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{asyncSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Summarize what ArcClaw is in one sentence, based on your training knowledge.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [SESSION-6] Poll status (run a few times until status is COMPLETED)
# Expect 200: status = IN_PROGRESS (while running) → COMPLETED (when done)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{asyncSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 3 — TERMINATE SESSION
# Wipes workspace directory and removes heartbeat registration.
# Idempotent — terminating an already-terminated session is safe.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SESSION-7] Terminate session — expect 204 No Content
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{mainSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SESSION-8] Terminate async session
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{asyncSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ERROR CASES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [SESSION-9] Status on non-existent session → expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/00000000-dead-beef-0000-000000000000/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [SESSION-10] Invalid request body — null goal → expect 400 (Bean Validation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": null,
    "agentRole": "",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [SESSION-11] Unknown agent role → expect 500 (IllegalArgumentException from AgentRoleEnum.fromString)
# Valid roles: coordinator | researcher | coder | debugger | architect | synthesizer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Hello",
    "agentRole": "unknown-role",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [SESSION-12] maxIterations hit — expect 408 LoopExceeded
# @name loopSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### Ask a multi-step question with maxIterations=1 to force loop exceeded
# Expect 408: {"reason":"Iteration limit 1 reached","code":"LOOP_EXCEEDED"}
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{loopSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Write a 500-word essay about the history of Java and then analyze its performance characteristics.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{loopSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###
